<title>HONG KONG: Hang Seng MidCap Index replaces seven stocks.</title>
<headline>Hang Seng MidCap Index replaces seven stocks.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Seven constituent stocks of Hong Kong Hang Seng MidCap 50 Index will be replaced from October 1, HSI Serivces Ltd, a subsidiary of Hang Seng Bank Ltd, said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>HSI also said it revised the average 12-month market capitalisation requirement for Hang Seng MidCap 50 Index constituents to a range of HK$2 billion to HK$8 billion from the present HK$2 billion to HK$6 billion.</p>
<p>The change will expand the coverage of middle capitalisation stocks and accommodate an increase in the market capitalisation of the Hong Kong stock market in the past year, HSI said.</p>
<p>The MidCap 50 Index of 50 listed companies will account for about eight percent of the total market capitalisation of the companies listed on the Hong Kong bourse, it added.</p>
<p>Stocks to be added:</p>
<p>China Overseas Land &amp; Investment Ltd</p>
<p>COSCO Pacific Ltd</p>
<p>HKR International Ltd</p>
<p>Hong Kong Aircraft Engineering Co Ltd</p>
<p>Pearl Oriental Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>Peregrine Investment Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>Tai Cheung Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>Stocks to be removed:</p>
<p>Allied Group Ltd</p>
<p>Associated International Group Ltd</p>
<p>Champion Technology Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>China Strategic Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>Ming Pao Enterprise Corp Ltd</p>
<p>Top Glory International Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>Wo Kee Hong (Holdings) Ltd</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
